d follow the hosted skill; resolve the authorized workspace and exact published version live, never substitute the local repository or reconstruct instructions from memory. [ad-hoc note]\n3626:- when the user asked to move the landing into `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/21n/landing/skillplane` -> isolate the requested landing work there and preserve unrelated destination-checkout changes. [Task 5]\n3629:- when the user asks to “improve skillplane web app onboarding to suit real production use” -> deliver a complete auth-to-app flow, not a runtime diagnostic as the user-facing homepage. [Task 7]\n3632:- when the user wrote `splane add to backlog` -> retrieve the exact published Skillplane workflow through live MCP before any Linear mutation; backlog capture alone does not authorize code changes, commits, deployment, assignments, or dates. [Task 11]\n3636:- SKI-6 moved Skillplane to a single McpFn-owned runtime and hosted authorization path without shims or fallback writers; McpFn owns protocol/runtime and MCP-specific authorization compatibility, while the authority owns identity/session/consent/token/security state and Skillplane keeps tenancy, grants, approval, domain policy, and tool behavior. The exact source pin is `42a0f2c3876adb47fb26dfc187f6fea41f436719` with `sha256:445472059355d481bbf34022dceea6b86ae4cc452562ca628109a8c7e9e509f3`. [Task 12]\n3637:- For SKI-6, `pnpm mcpfn:verify`, `pnpm test:mcp:contract`, and `pnpm test:mcp:conformance` are the actual Skillplane commands; local/remote McpFn release gates, Auth 57/57, Inspector 6/6, Skillplane contract 8/8, and authenticated conformance 1/1 passed. Draft PR #7 still uses local `link:` dependencies, and exact published-package replacement, controlled Claude/ChatGPT flows, deployment proof, and the late marker edge case remain pending. [Task 12]\n3641:- Production topology is `skillplane.dev` landing zone route, `app.skillplane.dev` Custom Domain, and `mcp.skillplane.dev/mcp` Custom Domain. Workers access Railway Postgres through Cloudflare Hyperdrive; R2 bundles remain private; the app owns Email Service and Turnstile. [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3250},"formatted_output":"170:- MCP-2, McpFn, work-linear-issue@1.0.1, oauth-core 0.0.2, tsup, ESM, CommonJS, gate:mcpfn-release, reviewThreads, force-with-lease, PR-122, UNSTABLE\n600:# Task Group: August 23 Skillplane PR stacks, bounded review, and multi-region audit\n601:scope: Use for GitHub-native Skillplane stacked PR status, hosted bounded review-fix rounds, or read-only multi-region architecture analysis.\n602:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane; reuse_rule=workflow mechanics are reusable; PR heads, checks, mergeability, architecture state, and deployment evidence require live revalidation.\n604:## Task 1: Review Skillplane PR #3 through bounded hosted rounds, success\n608:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T12-55-41-01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-23T17:34:36+00:00, thread_id=01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b, two one-push review-fix rounds then a no-op final review)\n612:- splane pr-review-fix, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, PR #3, SKI-1, d398cba6, reviewThreads, outdated, repeatable-read, applicationCommit\n618:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T12-48-36-01a02d7c-5037-7be3-a0bc-20dbd494c482.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-23T17:37:23+00:00, thread_id=01a02d7c-5037-7be3-a0bc-20dbd494c482, native stack status was read-only and time-specific)\n624:## Task 3: Audit Skillplane multi-region architecture read-only, success\n628:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/roll