{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T14:21:03.170Z","ordinal":15918,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a041ae-ce65-7631-a9e6-9a4d22e9067d","turn_id":"01a04de4-b2d2-7b13-8755-cb4387b230b8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-85132007-08c3-40e5-b390-ee54573e4f9a","process_id":"25790","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,280p' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,280p' /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md","name":"REDACTED.md","path":"/Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/2026-08-23T07-25-41-otTR-skillplane_pr3_bounded_review_fix_rounds.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"thread_id: 01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b\nupdated_at: 2026-08-23T17:34:36+00:00\nrollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T12-55-41-01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b.jsonl\ncwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane\ngit_branch: SKI-8\n\n# Bounded hosted Skillplane PR review-fix rounds for PR #3\n\nRollout context: In `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane`, the user repeatedly invoked `splane pr-review-fix` for `21nCo/skillplane` PR #3. The live Skillplane workflow resolved to `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` (published digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`). It mandates one bounded review snapshot, exact PR worktree validation, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and no post-push review refetch or CI loop.\n\n## Task 1: Initial report-and-fix review of PR #3\n\nOutcome: success\n\nPreference signals:\n\n- The user’s `splane pr review fixes PR #3` invocation was interpreted as a request to use the hosted Skillplane workflow, not local instructions or memory -> future `splane <skill>` commands should resolve and retrieve the live published skill first.\n- The workflow and prior user conventions required preserving a dirty checkout, using an exact-head dedicated worktree, and not overwriting unrelated artifacts -> review work was isolated at `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review` while the dirty `SKI-8` checkout remained untouched.\n- The hosted `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0` instructions required writing a raw evidence export and report before source edits, leaving code changes unstaged, and avoiding GitHub mutations; later `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` explicitly authorized one commit and push -> distinguish these workflow variants before acting.\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Discovered workspace `21n` via live Skillplane MCP and resolved `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`.\n- Confirmed PR #3 is `21nCo/skillplane`, head branch `SKI-1`, starting head `45733752797a5de552a447560983d24a9d02bcd1`; created a detached exact-head worktree.\n- Fetched all review surfaces once: 35 changed files, 21 inline comments, 6 submitted reviews, and 6 conversation comments. Stored `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n- Deduplicated review findings and validated them against current code. Addressed the then-current findings around rollup preservation, repeatable-read stats testing, and migration/application compatibility locking.\n- Added commit `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2` (`fix(review): harden stats rollout compatibility`) and pushed it to `SKI-1`.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n\n- PR #3 concerns AuthFn-backed service-principal credentials, public usage statistics, analytics rollups, and production deployment safety.\n- The repository’s production migration runner wraps migrations in transactions; migration `0019_public_stats_counter_shards.sql` changes public stats from one global counter to workspace shards. The implemented deployment guard records `applicationCommit` in production migration state and requires the deployment source commit to match it, preventing older binaries from running against the migrated schema.\n- Rollup preservation must use `existing.source_event_count >= eventCount` and return the persisted count, otherwise retention can erase fuller historical snapshots or make `RollupResult.sourceEvents` inconsistent.\n- The public-stats integration test previously held `LOCK TABLE skills IN SHARE MODE` across an HTTP request. The fix used a repeatable-read transaction and a same-connection app service provider; a read-only transaction failed because API middleware writes rate-limit state, so writable repeatable-read is required.\n- Focused validation passed: audit analytics 3/3, public-skills 5/5, observability tests 5/5, typechecks, lint/format/diff checks, full unit suite 28/28 Turbo tasks and 23/23 script tests.\n\nFailures and how to do differently:\n\n- An initial raw-export patch failed because the generated `apply_patch` string lacked the exact final `*** End Patch` line; retry with a correctly terminated patch.\n- A same-connection test attempt returned 503 because `createApiApp` requires `getServices`, not a services object. A second attempt returned 500 because `READ ONLY` blocked middleware writes. Correct wiring plus writable repeatable-read produced the passing test.\n- The immediate PR metadata check after push still showed the prior SHA even though local and remote refs matched. Do not poll or refetch in a bounded round; report the refresh lag honestly.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1`, digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`.\n- PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n- Worktree: `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review`.\n- Report export: `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n- Commit: `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2`.\n\n## Task 2: Follow-up bounded review round\n\nOutcome: success\n\nPreference signals:\n\n- The user invoked `splane pr-review-fix` again, implicitly requesting another bounded hosted round rather than an open-ended loop -> fetch once, fix once, push once, and terminate.\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Retrieved the current published `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` skill again and verified clean `SKI-1` worktree/local/remote head at `996aebe...`.\n- Current review snapshot identified one actionable test gap: the compatibility test title claimed coverage for an unversioned application, but the test only covered an unversioned migration record.\n- Added an assertion calling `assertMigrationApplicationCompatibility({ applicationCommit: \"a\".repeat(40) })` without an application argument.\n- Ran formatting, lint, diff checks, and focused deployment tests (2/2 passed).\n- Created and pushed exactly one commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6` (`test(review): cover unversioned application deploys`). Local and remote matched; immediate PR metadata again lagged.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Added test: `scripts/production-deployment.test.mjs`.\n- Commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n\n## Task 3: Final bounded review round\n\nOutcome: success\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Retrieved the hosted workflow again and verified the dedicated worktree was clean with local, remote, and PR head all at `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n- Fetched review threads and supplementary surfaces once. There were 18 unresolved threads, but 7 were outdated; the current recent test comment was marked addressed by `d398cba`.\n- Read current code for remaining threads. No new actionable findings were found, so no files changed, commit was created, or push performed.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n\n- Unresolved GitHub thread status alone is insufficient: inspect `outdated`, current commit, current code, and explicit addressed markers. Current threads may be historical but already fixed or intentionally retained contracts.\n- Remaining not-attempted/intentional items included local expiry delegation to AuthFn, immutable applied migrations, and inability to reconstruct irrecoverable pre-counter historical data.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Final PR head: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n- Final PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n- Final result: no-op round; no tests rerun because no files changed.\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"thread_id: 01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b\nupdated_at: 2026-08-23T17:34:36+00:00\nrollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T12-55-41-01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b.jsonl\ncwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane\ngit_branch: SKI-8\n\n# Bounded hosted Skillplane PR review-fix rounds for PR #3\n\nRollout context: In `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane`, the user repeatedly invoked `splane pr-review-fix` for `21nCo/skillplane` PR #3. The live Skillplane workflow resolved to `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` (published digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`). It mandates one bounded review snapshot, exact PR worktree validation, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and no post-push review refetch or CI loop.\n\n## Task 1: Initial report-and-fix review of PR #3\n\nOutcome: success\n\nPreference signals:\n\n- The user’s `splane pr review fixes PR #3` invocation was interpreted as a request to use the hosted Skillplane workflow, not local instructions or memory -> future `splane <skill>` commands should resolve and retrieve the live published skill first.\n- The workflow and prior user conventions required preserving a dirty checkout, using an exact-head dedicated worktree, and not overwriting unrelated artifacts -> review work was isolated at `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review` while the dirty `SKI-8` checkout remained untouched.\n- The hosted `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0` instructions required writing a raw evidence export and report before source edits, leaving code changes unstaged, and avoiding GitHub mutations; later `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` explicitly authorized one commit and push -> distinguish these workflow variants before acting.\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Discovered workspace `21n` via live Skillplane MCP and resolved `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`.\n- Confirmed PR #3 is `21nCo/skillplane`, head branch `SKI-1`, starting head `45733752797a5de552a447560983d24a9d02bcd1`; created a detached exact-head worktree.\n- Fetched all review surfaces once: 35 changed files, 21 inline comments, 6 submitted reviews, and 6 conversation comments. Stored `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n- Deduplicated review findings and validated them against current code. Addressed the then-current findings around rollup preservation, repeatable-read stats testing, and migration/application compatibility locking.\n- Added commit `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2` (`fix(review): harden stats rollout compatibility`) and pushed it to `SKI-1`.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n\n- PR #3 concerns AuthFn-backed service-principal credentials, public usage statistics, analytics rollups, and production deployment safety.\n- The repository’s production migration runner wraps migrations in transactions; migration `0019_public_stats_counter_shards.sql` changes public stats from one global counter to workspace shards. The implemented deployment guard records `applicationCommit` in production migration state and requires the deployment source commit to match it, preventing older binaries from running against the migrated schema.\n- Rollup preservation must use `existing.source_event_count >= eventCount` and return the persisted count, otherwise retention can erase fuller historical snapshots or make `RollupResult.sourceEvents` inconsistent.\n- The public-stats integration test previously held `LOCK TABLE skills IN SHARE MODE` across an HTTP request. The fix used a repeatable-read transaction and a same-connection app service provider; a read-only transaction failed because API middleware writes rate-limit state, so writable repeatable-read is required.\n- Focused validation passed: audit analytics 3/3, public-skills 5/5, observability tests 5/5, typechecks, lint/format/diff checks, full unit suite 28/28 Turbo tasks and 23/23 script tests.\n\nFailures and how to do differently:\n\n- An initial raw-export patch failed because the generated `apply_patch` string lacked the exact final `*** End Patch` line; retry with a correctly terminated patch.\n- A same-connection test attempt returned 503 because `createApiApp` requires `getServices`, not a services object. A second attempt returned 500 because `READ ONLY` blocked middleware writes. Correct wiring plus writable repeatable-read produced the passing test.\n- The immediate PR metadata check after push still showed the prior SHA even though local and remote refs matched. Do not poll or refetch in a bounded round; report the refresh lag honestly.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1`, digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`.\n- PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n- Worktree: `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review`.\n- Report export: `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n- Commit: `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2`.\n\n## Task 2: Follow-up bounded review round\n\nOutcome: success\n\nPreference signals:\n\n- The user invoked `splane pr-review-fix` again, implicitly requesting another bounded hosted round rather than an open-ended loop -> fetch once, fix once, push once, and terminate.\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Retrieved the current published `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` skill again and verified clean `SKI-1` worktree/local/remote head at `996aebe...`.\n- Current review snapshot identified one actionable test gap: the compatibility test title claimed coverage for an unversioned application, but the test only covered an unversioned migration record.\n- Added an assertion calling `assertMigrationApplicationCompatibility({ applicationCommit: \"a\".repeat(40) })` without an application argument.\n- Ran formatting, lint, diff checks, and focused deployment tests (2/2 passed).\n- Created and pushed exactly one commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6` (`test(review): cover unversioned application deploys`). Local and remote matched; immediate PR metadata again lagged.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Added test: `scripts/production-deployment.test.mjs`.\n- Commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n\n## Task 3: Final bounded review round\n\nOutcome: success\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Retrieved the hosted workflow again and verified the dedicated worktree was clean with local, remote, and PR head all at `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n- Fetched review threads and supplementary surfaces once. There were 18 unresolved threads, but 7 were outdated; the current recent test comment was marked addressed by `d398cba`.\n- Read current code for remaining threads. No new actionable findings were found, so no files changed, commit was created, or push performed.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n\n- Unresolved GitHub thread status alone is insufficient: inspect `outdated`, current commit, current code, and explicit addressed markers. Current threads may be historical but already fixed or intentionally retained contracts.\n- Remaining not-attempted/intentional items included local expiry delegation to AuthFn, immutable applied migrations, and inability to reconstruct irrecoverable pre-counter historical data.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Final PR head: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n- Final PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n- Final result: no-op round; no tests rerun because no files changed.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4167},"formatted_output":"thread_id: 01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b\nupdated_at: 2026-08-23T17:34:36+00:00\nrollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T12-55-41-01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b.jsonl\ncwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane\ngit_branch: SKI-8\n\n# Bounded hosted Skillplane PR review-fix rounds for PR #3\n\nRollout context: In `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane`, the user repeatedly invoked `splane pr-review-fix` for `21nCo/skillplane` PR #3. The live Skillplane workflow resolved to `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` (published digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`). It mandates one bounded review snapshot, exact PR worktree validation, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and no post-push review refetch or CI loop.\n\n## Task 1: Initial report-and-fix review of PR #3\n\nOutcome: success\n\nPreference signals:\n\n- The user’s `splane pr review fixes PR #3` invocation was interpreted as a request to use the hosted Skillplane workflow, not local instructions or memory -> future `splane <skill>` commands should resolve and retrieve the live published skill first.\n- The workflow and prior user conventions required preserving a dirty checkout, using an exact-head dedicated worktree, and not overwriting unrelated artifacts -> review work was isolated at `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review` while the dirty `SKI-8` checkout remained untouched.\n- The hosted `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0` instructions required writing a raw evidence export and report before source edits, leaving code changes unstaged, and avoiding GitHub mutations; later `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` explicitly authorized one commit and push -> distinguish these workflow variants before acting.\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Discovered workspace `21n` via live Skillplane MCP and resolved `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`.\n- Confirmed PR #3 is `21nCo/skillplane`, head branch `SKI-1`, starting head `45733752797a5de552a447560983d24a9d02bcd1`; created a detached exact-head worktree.\n- Fetched all review surfaces once: 35 changed files, 21 inline comments, 6 submitted reviews, and 6 conversation comments. Stored `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n- Deduplicated review findings and validated them against current code. Addressed the then-current findings around rollup preservation, repeatable-read stats testing, and migration/application compatibility locking.\n- Added commit `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2` (`fix(review): harden stats rollout compatibility`) and pushed it to `SKI-1`.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n\n- PR #3 concerns AuthFn-backed service-principal credentials, public usage statistics, analytics rollups, and production deployment safety.\n- The repository’s production migration runner wraps migrations in transactions; migration `0019_public_stats_counter_shards.sql` changes public stats from one global counter to workspace shards. The implemented deployment guard records `applicationCommit` in production migration state and requires the deployment source commit to match it, preventing older binaries from running against the migrated schema.\n- Rollup preservation must use `existing.source_event_count >= eventCount` and return the persisted count, otherwise retention can erase fuller historical snapshots or make `RollupResult.sourceEvents` inconsistent.\n- The public-stats integration test previously held `LOCK TABLE skills IN SHARE MODE` across an HTTP request. The fix used a repeatable-read transaction and a same-connection app service provider; a read-only transaction failed because API middleware writes rate-limit state, so writable repeatable-read is required.\n- Focused validation passed: audit analytics 3/3, public-skills 5/5, observability tests 5/5, typechecks, lint/format/diff checks, full unit suite 28/28 Turbo tasks and 23/23 script tests.\n\nFailures and how to do differently:\n\n- An initial raw-export patch failed because the generated `apply_patch` string lacked the exact final `*** End Patch` line; retry with a correctly terminated patch.\n- A same-connection test attempt returned 503 because `createApiApp` requires `getServices`, not a services object. A second attempt returned 500 because `READ ONLY` blocked middleware writes. Correct wiring plus writable repeatable-read produced the passing test.\n- The immediate PR metadata check after push still showed the prior SHA even though local and remote refs matched. Do not poll or refetch in a bounded round; report the refresh lag honestly.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1`, digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`.\n- PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n- Worktree: `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review`.\n- Report export: `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n- Commit: `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2`.\n\n## Task 2: Follow-up bounded review round\n\nOutcome: success\n\nPreference signals:\n\n- The user invoked `splane pr-review-fix` again, implicitly requesting another bounded hosted round rather than an open-ended loop -> fetch once, fix once, push once, and terminate.\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Retrieved the current published `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` skill again and verified clean `SKI-1` worktree/local/remote head at `996aebe...`.\n- Current review snapshot identified one actionable test gap: the compatibility test title claimed coverage for an unversioned application, but the test only covered an unversioned migration record.\n- Added an assertion calling `assertMigrationApplicationCompatibility({ applicationCommit: \"a\".repeat(40) })` without an application argument.\n- Ran formatting, lint, diff checks, and focused deployment tests (2/2 passed).\n- Created and pushed exactly one commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6` (`test(review): cover unversioned application deploys`). Local and remote matched; immediate PR metadata again lagged.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Added test: `scripts/production-deployment.test.mjs`.\n- Commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n\n## Task 3: Final bounded review round\n\nOutcome: success\n\nKey steps:\n\n- Retrieved the hosted workflow again and verified the dedicated worktree was clean with local, remote, and PR head all at `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n- Fetched review threads and supplementary surfaces once. There were 18 unresolved threads, but 7 were outdated; the current recent test comment was marked addressed by `d398cba`.\n- Read current code for remaining threads. No new actionable findings were found, so no files changed, commit was created, or push performed.\n\nReusable knowledge:\n\n- Unresolved GitHub thread status alone is insufficient: inspect `outdated`, current commit, current code, and explicit addressed markers. Current threads may be historical but already fixed or intentionally retained contracts.\n- Remaining not-attempted/intentional items included local expiry delegation to AuthFn, immutable applied migrations, and inability to reconstruct irrecoverable pre-counter historical data.\n\nReferences:\n\n- Final PR head: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n- Final PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n- Final result: no-op round; no tests rerun because no files changed.\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1788013263170,"completed_at_ms":1788013263170}}
