space and exact published Skillplane skill live through MCP; do not substitute local repository instructions or reconstruct the skill from memory. [ad-hoc note]\n   637\t- when `splane pr-review-fix` is invoked repeatedly -> each invocation is a new bounded hosted round: fetch once, fix/verify once, push at most once, then terminate. [Task 1]\n   638\t- when the user says “I didn't do anything locally ... only did it on PR in Github” -> explain GitHub UI-created stacks without assuming local CLI setup. [Task 2]\n   639\t- for a “read-only audit” -> preserve dirty state and report without edits, deployments, or log mutations. [Task 3]\n   640\t\n   641\t## Reusable knowledge\n   642\t\n   643\t- `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` uses unresolved GraphQL threads plus review bodies, issue comments, and inline comments as one snapshot; after an authorized push, verify heads once and do not refetch/poll. An unresolved thread can be historical: inspect `outdated`, current code/commit, and addressed markers. [Task 1]\n   644\t- Related skill: `skills/thread-aware-pr-review-triage/SKILL.md`. [Task 1]\n   645\t- GitHub-native stacks do not require Graphite or local setup: child PRs target the branch below. A lower-branch change can diverge upper PRs; use GitHub’s Rebase stack before calling the stack merge-ready, while treating actual PR status/checks as live-only. [Task 2]\n   646\t- Skillplane’s recommended target is central AuthFn/OAuth/workspace-directory authorization followed by `workspace_id -> region_id/routing_epoch`, a short-lived internal assertion, and private Service Binding forwarding to regional single-writer workspace cells. Reject stale routes with `409 WORKSPACE_REGION_MISMATCH` before side effects. [Task 3]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":1167},"formatted_output":"   600\t# Task Group: August 23 Skillplane PR stacks, bounded review, and multi-region audit\n   601\tscope: Use for GitHub-native Skillplane stacked PR status, hosted bounded review-fix ro