` at `c13917c360b326d6199162de63df9e61e4885944`\\n+- McpFn source: local `MCP-2` worktree at base `9134bb13f9682b5debc14d69d5927de0be2274e1`\\n+- McpFn source digest: `sha256:51bf866cc5ec5cb0ba3dee17fdbbd589f3dcaeab388c9685c25828fbde252da9`\\n+- Publication state: publication authorized on `codex/ski-6-mcpfn-runtime`; merge, deployment, live-provider verification, and Linear status transition remain out of scope\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n- McpFn source: local `MCP-2` worktree at base `42a0f2c3876adb47fb26dfc187f6fea41f436719`\\n- McpFn source digest: `sha256:445472059355d481bbf34022dceea6b86ae4cc452562ca628109a8c7e9e509f3`\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f512980`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f512980e42247b92388bc72185d92f9869ce51fa)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696560\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696563,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/src/auth.ts\",\n    \"line\": 253,\n    \"original_line\": 253,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=39a2e46b-cfa5-4e41-8da5-9abf8b5e44d3 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: When the Authorization header is malformed, `readBearerToken` can throw before `authenticateMcpRequest` creates an `McpAuthenticationError`, so `/downloads/:grant` returns 500 instead of the required 401 authentication response. Restore the parser error conversion around this call.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/src/auth.ts, line 250:\\n\\n<comment>When the Authorization header is malformed, `readBearerToken` can throw before `authenticateMcpRequest` creates an `McpAuthenticationError`, so `/downloads/:grant` returns 500 instead of the required 401 authentication response. Restore the parser error conversion around this call.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -234,11 +233,29 @@ export async function authenticateMcpRequest(\\n+  services: ApiServices,\\n+  additionalScopes: readonly McpScope[] = [],\\n+): Promise<McpIdentity> {\\n+  const token = readBearerToken(request);\\n+  if (!token) {\\n+    throw new McpAuthenticationError(401, \\\"A valid bearer credential is required\\\");\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  let token: string | undefined;\\n  try {\\n    token = readBearerToken(request);\\n  } catch {\\n    throw new McpAuthenticationError(401, \\\"A valid bearer credential is required\\\");\\n  }\\n  if (!token) {\\n    throw new McpAuthenticationError(401, \\\"A valid bearer credential is required\\\");\\n  }\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696563\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696571,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:52Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 56,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=6dc0ea3d-8a73-4706-a735-278feed06f69 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP2: On Windows, the fixed `sourceDigest` cannot match a digest generated on Unix because `relative()` contributes native backslashes to the hash. Normalize digest labels to `/` before hashing.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs, line 56:\\n\\n<comment>On Windows, the fixed `sourceDigest` cannot match a digest generated on Unix because `relative()` contributes native backslashes to the hash. Normalize digest labels to `/` before hashing.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@\\n+  ].toSorted((left, right) => left.localeCompare(right));\\n+  for (const path of files) {\\n+    const content = await readFile(path);\\n+    const label = relative(sourceRoot, path);\\n+    digest.update(label).update(\\\"\\\\0\\\").update(String(content.byteLength)).update(\\\"\\\\0\\\");\\n+    digest.update(content);\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f9bc1d8`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696571\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696574,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:54Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 10,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=bcf545c6-26b4-487f-9a42-3232e2d36e67 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: On non-Windows systems without Git at exactly `/usr/bin/git`, `pnpm mcpfn:verify` fails even when `git` is available on `PATH`. Invoke `git` by name so the adoption gate works with the repository's supported development environments.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs, line 10:\\n\\n<comment>On no