nce\\\":8} -->\\nP1: Verify the linked packages' resolved runtime artifacts, or rebuild and compare them reproducibly. `mcpfn:verify` currently hashes only `package.json` and `src/**`, so stale or modified exported `dist` files can execute while the gate passes.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs, line 50:\\n\\n<comment>Verify the linked packages' resolved runtime artifacts, or rebuild and compare them reproducibly. `mcpfn:verify` currently hashes only `package.json` and `src/**`, so stale or modified exported `dist` files can execute while the gate passes.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@\\n+  if (packageJson.name !== name || packageJson.version !== packageContract.version) {\\n+    fail(`${name} package identity does not match mcpfn-source.json`);\\n+  }\\n+  const files = [\\n+    packageJsonPath,\\n+    ...(await sourceFiles(resolve(packageRoot, \\\"src\\\"))),\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696549\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696550,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 153,\n    \"original_line\": 109,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=61d1bc0f-4515-4341-8b9d-3164a85bc984 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP1: Apply the IP/request rate limit before McpFn resolves a client metadata document. The limiter is inside the token-authority callback, so invalid HTTPS `client_id` requests can trigger `runtime.fetcher` before Skillplane rate-limits `/authorize` or `/token`.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts, line 109:\\n\\n<comment>Apply the IP/request rate limit before McpFn resolves a client metadata document. The limiter is inside the token-authority callback, so invalid HTTPS `client_id` requests can trigger `runtime.fetcher` before Skillplane rate-limits `/authorize` or `/token`.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -150,64 +45,128 @@ async function token(runtime: OAuthRuntime, request: Request): Promise<Response>\\n+    tokenAuthority: {\\n+      exchangeAuthorizationCode: (input, request) =>\\n+        fromTokenAuthority(async () => {\\n+          await tokenRateLimit(runtime, input.client.clientId, request);\\n+          const tokens = await exchangeAuthorizationCode(runtime, {\\n+            code: input.code,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696550\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696552,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 166,\n    \"original_line\": 121,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=61620626-d95e-4367-afff-199266e941bf -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP2: Refresh-token requests no longer consume the shared `oauth-token:*` limiter because this callback calls only `exchangeRefreshToken`. The previous token route applied that limiter before both grant branches, so refresh traffic can now use a separate bucket and exceed the former combined token limit. Call `tokenRateLimit` here as well.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts, line 121:\\n\\n<comment>Refresh-token requests no longer consume the shared `oauth-token:*` limiter because this callback calls only `exchangeRefreshToken`. The previous token route applied that limiter before both grant branches, so refresh traffic can now use a separate bucket and exceed the former combined token limit. Call `tokenRateLimit` here as well.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -150,64 +45,128 @@ async function token(runtime: OAuthRuntime, request: Request): Promise<Response>\\n+        }),\\n+      refreshToken: (input, request) =>\\n+        fromTokenAuthority(async () => {\\n+          const tokens = await exchangeRefreshToken(runtime, {\\n+            refreshToken: input.refreshToken,\\n+            clientId: input.client.clientId,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n          await tokenRateLimit(runtime, input.client.clientId, request);\\n          const tokens = await exchangeRefreshToken(runtime, {\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696552\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696557,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:59Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/package.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 16,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=caa37ec4-b246-420c-93fb-45795e983e34 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: The added `@mcpfn/*` dependencies use machine-specific `link:` paths that resolve to `/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/...` at the filesystem root. That directory exists only on your local machine, so `pnpm install` fails on a fresh checkout, in CI, and for any other developer, blocking build/typecheck/test until it is manually recreated. The link specifier also carries no version, so pnpm resolves whatever sits at that path at install time; the pinned commit/digest from mcpfn-source.json is only checked when someone manually runs `pnpm mcpfn:verify`, which is not wired into CI or install. Until exact published @mcpfn packages exist, document this as required in CI/onboarding, and wire the `mcpfn:verify` gate into the CI install/verify step so the pin and digest are enforced automatically.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/package.json, line 16:\\n\\n<comment>The added `@mcpfn/*` dependencies use machine-specific `link:` paths that resolve to `/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/...` at the filesystem root. That directory exists only on your local machine, so `pnpm install` fails on a fresh checkout, in CI, and for any other developer, blocking build/typecheck/test until it is manually recreated. The link specifier also carries no version, so pnpm resolves whatever sits at that path at install time; the pinned commit/digest from mcpfn-source.json is only checked when someone manually runs `pnpm mcpfn:verify`, which is not wired into CI or install. Until exact published @mcpfn packages exist, document this as required in CI/onboarding, and wire the `mcpfn:verify` gate into the CI install/verify step so the pin and digest are enforced automatically.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@\\n     \\\"deploy:check\\\": \\\"wrangler deploy --config wrangler.jsonc --dry-run --outdir dist-worker\\\"\\n   },\\n   \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n+    \\\"@mcpfn/auth\\\": \\\"link:../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/auth\\\",\\n+    \\\"@mcpfn/core\\\": \\\"link:../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/core\\\",\\n     \\\"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f9bc1d8`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696557\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696560,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T07:22:56Z\",\n    \"path\": \".conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 12,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=76bf5ff2-d5ce-4953-985a-9dcb031de456 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: The recorded McpFn pin (base `9134bb13...`, digest `sha256:51bf...`) does not match the enforced pin in `mcpfn-source.json` (base `42a0f2c3...`, digest `sha256:4454...`), which `pnpm mcpfn:verify` and the release gates verify against. Since this completion record's purpose is to document the exact verified source, the wrong base/digest pair will mislead anyone re-verifying or later replacing the pin. Correct lines 11-12 (and the matching reference in the Verification section) to record the repository's actual pinned base commit and source digest.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At .conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md, line 11:\\n\\n<comment>The recorded McpFn pin (base `9134bb13...`, digest `sha256:51bf...`) does not match the enforced pin in `mcpfn-source.json` (base `42a0f2c3...`, digest `sha256:4454...`), which `pnpm mcpfn:verify` and the release gates verify against. Since this completion record's purpose is to document the exact verified source, the wrong base/digest pair will mislead anyone re-verifying or later replacing the pin. Correct lines 11-12 (and the matching reference in the Verification section) to record the repository's actual pinned base commit and source digest.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@\\n+- Launcher: `Codex Desktop`\\n+- Issue: Linear `SKI-6` — Adopt McpFn for Skillplane MCP runtime, authorization, and quality gates\\n+- Skillplane base: `main` at `c13917c360b326d6199162de63df9e61e4885944`\\n+- McpFn source: local `MCP-2` worktree at base `9134bb13f9682b5debc14d69d5927de0be2274e1`\\n+- McpFn source digest: `sha256:51bf866cc5ec5cb0ba3dee17fdbbd589f3dcaeab388c9685c25828fbde252da9`\\n+- Publication state: publication authorized on `codex/ski-6-mcpfn-runtime`; merge, deployment, live-provider verification, and Linear status transition remain out of scope\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n- McpFn source: local `MCP-2` worktree at base `42a0f2c3876adb47fb26dfc187f6fea41f436719`\\n- McpFn source digest: `sha256:445472059355d481bbf34022dceea6b86ae4cc452562ca628109a8c7e9e509f3`\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f512980`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f512980e42247b92388bc72185d92f9869ce51fa)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696560\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696563,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/src/auth.ts\",\n    \"line\": 253,\n    \"original_line\": 253,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=39a2e46b-cfa5-4e41-8da5-9abf8b5e44d3 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: When the Authorization header is malformed, `readBearerToken` can throw before `authenticateMcpRequest` creates an `McpAuthenticationError`, so `/downloads/:grant` returns 500 instead of the required 401 authentication response. Restore the parser error conversion around this call.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/src/auth.ts, line 250:\\n\\n<comment>When the Authorization header is malformed, `readBearerToken` can throw before `authenticateMcpRequest` creates an `McpAuthenticationError`, so `/downloads/:grant` returns 500 instead of the required 401 authentication response. Restore the parser error conversion around this call.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -234,11 +233,29 @@ export async function authenticateMcpRequest(\\n+  services: ApiServices,\\n+  additionalScopes: readonly McpScope[] = [],\\n+): Promise<McpIdentity> {\\n+  const token = readBearerToken(request);\\n+  if (!token) {\\n+    throw new McpAuthenticationError(401, \\\"A valid bearer credential is required\\\");\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  let token: string | undefined;\\n  try {\\n    token = readBearerToken(request);\\n  } catch {\\n    throw new McpAuthenticationError(401, \\\"A valid bearer credential is required\\\");\\n  }\\n  if (!token) {\\n    throw new McpAuthenticationError(401, \\\"A valid bearer credential is required\\\");\\n  }\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696563\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696571,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:52Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 56,\n    \"