 null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=bcf545c6-26b4-487f-9a42-3232e2d36e67 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: On non-Windows systems without Git at exactly `/usr/bin/git`, `pnpm mcpfn:verify` fails even when `git` is available on `PATH`. Invoke `git` by name so the adoption gate works with the repository's supported development environments.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs, line 10:\\n\\n<comment>On non-Windows systems without Git at exactly `/usr/bin/git`, `pnpm mcpfn:verify` fails even when `git` is available on `PATH`. Invoke `git` by name so the adoption gate works with the repository's supported development environments.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@\\n+import { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\n+\\n+const repoRoot = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \\\"..\\\");\\n+const gitExecutable =\\n+  process.platform === \\\"win32\\\"\\n+    ? \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Program Files\\\\\\\\Git\\\\\\\\cmd\\\\\\\\git.exe\\\"\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f9bc1d8`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696574\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696576,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \".conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json\",\n    \"line\": 21,\n    \"original_line\": 21,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=e267f1dc-112e-4c60-a9c5-2186b62f63b3 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: The `expectedFailureScenarios` list does not match the actual failing checks in the same document. It names `elicitation-sep1034-defaults` and `elicitation-sep1330-enums`, but the checks array reports FAILURE for `elicitation-sep1034-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (the `-defaults`/`-enums` IDs do not appear anywhere in `result.checks`). Because the `interpretation` field claims exit code zero means every failure or warning belongs to the documented baseline, two actual failures are left outside the baseline list and two listed entries reference non-existent check IDs. Update the two elicitation IDs to the `-general` variants actually reported by the runner so the summary accurately documents the conformance baseline.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At .conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json, line 21:\\n\\n<comment>The `expectedFailureScenarios` list does not match the actual failing checks in the same document. It names `elicitation-sep1034-defaults` and `elicitation-sep1330-enums`, but the checks array reports FAILURE for `elicitation-sep1034-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (the `-defaults`/`-enums` IDs do not appear anywhere in `result.checks`). Because the `interpretation` field claims exit code zero means every failure or warning belongs to the documented baseline, two actual failures are left outside the baseline list and two listed entries reference non-existent check IDs. Update the two elicitation IDs to the `-general` variants actually reported by the runner so the summary accurately documents the conformance baseline.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@\\n+    \\\"tools-call-sampling\\\",\\n+    \\\"tools-call-elicitation\\\",\\n+    \\\"server-sse-multiple-streams\\\",\\n+    \\\"elicitation-sep1034-defaults\\\",\\n+    \\\"elicitation-sep1330-enums\\\",\\n+    \\\"resources-list\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    \\\"elicitation-sep1034-general\\\",\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696576\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696580,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/tests/conformance/expected-failures.yml\",\n    \"line\": 23,\n    \"original_line\": 23,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=6f7847df-9c0a-4408-8d58-85250473f5e0 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: The expected-failure scenario ids here do not match the ids recorded by the actual conformance run in `.conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json`. Three entries are wrong: the summary records FAILURE ids `elicitation-sep1034-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (not `elicitation-sep1034-defaults` / `elicitation-sep1330-enums`), and the baselined SSE warning id is `server-sse-multiple-streams-session` (not `server-sse-multiple-streams`). The file comment says the SSE session warning is baselined explicitly, so the entry is missing its `-session` suffix. Because the baseline id is not the id the runner emitted, the gate either does not actually baseline the intended scenario (exact match) or baselines a name that never occurs, so the recorded \\\"every failure/warning belongs to the baseline\\\" evidence does not reconcile with these entries. Align each entry with the exact scenario ids emitted by the conformance runner and re-verify the gate stays green.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/tests/conformance/expected-failures.yml, line 21:\\n\\n<comment>The expected-failure scenario ids here do not match the ids recorded by the actual conformance run in `.conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json`. Three entries are wrong: the summary records FAILURE ids `elicitation-sep1034-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (not `elicitation-sep1034-defaults` / `elicitation-sep1330-enums`), and the baselined SSE warning id is `server-sse-multiple-streams-session` (not `server-sse-multiple-streams`). The file comment says the SSE session warning is baselined explicitly, so the entry is missing its `-session` suffix. Because the baseline id is not the id the runner emitted, the gate either does not actually baseline the intended scenario (exact match) or baselines a name that never occurs, so the recorded \\\"every failure/warning belongs to the baseline\\\" evidence does not reconcile with these entries. Align each entry with the exact scenario ids emitted by the conformance runner and re-verify the gate stays green.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\\n+  - tools-call-with-progress\\n+  - tools-call-sampling\\n+  - tools-call-elicitation\\n+  - server-sse-multiple-streams\\n+  - elicitation-sep1034-defaults\\n+  - elicitation-sep1330-enums\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  - server-sse-multiple-streams-session\\n  - elicitation-sep1034-general\\n  - elicitation-sep1330-general\\n\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696580\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696583,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:58Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn-source.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 4,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=be7e1605-43b2-461a-8a15-e496f8ceb296 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} -->\\nP2: This pin and the `link:` dependencies it backs (mcp/package.json, packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/package.json) resolve to an external local worktree at `../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2`, which is outside the repository and not part of the checkout. `pnpm mcpfn:verify` runs `git -C <sourceRoot> rev-parse HEAD` and immediately throws, and `pnpm install` resolves each `link:` to a nonexistent directory. A clean checkout on any other machine or CI runner can therefore neither install/build nor pass the adoption gate — nothing in the repo or lockfile makes the pinned source reproducible. The draft-boundary limitation is acknowledged in the PR, but as written this file makes the committed state non-buildable; keep it as a draft-only boundary or vendor the exact commit into the repo until the published-package replacement lands.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn-source.json, line 4:\\n\\n<comment>This pin and the `link:` dependencies it backs (mcp/package.json, packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/package.json) resolve to an external local worktree at `../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2`, which is outside the repository and not part of the checkout. `pnpm mcpfn:verify` runs `git -C <sourceRoot> rev-parse HEAD` and immediately throws, and `pnpm install` resolves each `link:` to a nonexistent directory. A clean checkout on any other machine or CI runner can therefore neither install/build nor pass the adoption gate — nothing in the repo or lockfile makes the pinned source reproducible. The draft-boundary limitation is acknowledged in the PR, but as written this file makes the committed state non-buildable; keep it as a draft-only boundary or vendor the exact commit into the repo until the published-package replacement lands.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\\n+{\\n+  \\\"schemaVersion\\\": 1,\\n+  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"local-worktree\\\",\\n+  \\\"sourceRoot\\\": \\\"../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2\\\",\\n+  \\\"baseCommit\\\": \\\"42a0f2c3876adb47fb26dfc187f6fea41f436719\\\",\\n+  \\\"sourceDigest\\\": \\\"sha256:445472059355d481bbf34022dceea6b86ae4cc452562ca628109a8c7e9e509f3\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f9bc1d8`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696583\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696585,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 184,\n    \"original_line\": 121,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=d050964c-66a1-46c3-8faa-39b519b6fb56 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} -->\\nP2: The replacement redirect test drops most of the previous security coverage. The old `validateRedirectUri` suite rejected redirect URIs with userinfo credentials, URL fragments, and wildcard hosts, and the removed `validateRegistration` test asserted that confidential auth methods, non-code response types, password/other grants, and non-allowlisted scopes are rejected. The new `normalizeMcpClientRegistration` test only covers a single unsafe HTTP redirect URI plus one loopback/HTTPS normalization, so a regression in McpFn rejecting credentials, fragments, wildcards, client_secret_basic, implicit/password grants, or unknown scopes would not be caught. Restore equivalent rejection coverage for this security boundary.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts, line 121:\\n\\n<comment>The replacement redirect test drops most of the previous security coverage. The old `validateRedirectUri` suite rejected redirect URIs with userinfo credentials, URL fragments, and wildcard hosts, and the removed `validateRegistration` test asserted that confidential auth methods, non-code response types, password/other grants, and non-allowlisted scopes are rejected. The new `normalizeMcpClientRegistration` test only covers a single unsafe HTTP redirect URI plus one loopback/HTTPS normalization, so a regression in McpFn rejecting credentials, fragments, wildcards, client_secret_basic, implicit/password grants, or unknown scopes would not be caught. Restore equivalent rejection coverage for this security boundary.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -119,25 +118,28 @@ describe(\\\"OAuth 2.1 metadata and configuration\\\", () => {\\n-      \\\"https://agent.example.test/callback?source=mcp\\\",\\n-    );\\n-    expect(validateRedirectUri(\\\"http://127.0.0.1:49152/callback\\\")).toBe(\\n+  it(\\\"delegates exact HTTPS and loopback redirect normalization to McpFn\\\", () => {\\n+    const registration = normalizeMcpClientRegistration({\\n+      clientId: \\\"client\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696585\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696586,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/tests/conformance/mcp.official-conformance.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 89,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=183f8661-633b-4d6f-901f-a966f50af8cb -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: The forwarding server's `.catch(() => response.writeHead(500).end())` swallows the thrown error without logging it. When the app under test throws, the conformance runner sees a bare 500 and the root-cause stack trace is discarded, which costs debugging time when a boundary regression trips this suite. Log the error before returning the 500.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/tests/conformance/mcp.official-conformance.test.ts, line 89:\\n\\n<comment>The forwarding server's `.catch(() => response.writeHead(500).end())` swallows the thrown error without logging it. When the app under test throws, the conformance runner sees a bare 500 and the root-cause stack trace is discarded, which costs debugging time when a boundary regression trips this suite. Log the error before returning the 500.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,205 @@\\n+    void webRequest(request)\\n+      .then((converted) => environment.app.fetch(converted))\\n+      .then((result) => writeWebResponse(result, response))\\n+      .catch(() => response.writeHead(500).end());\\n+  });\\n+  await new Promise<void>((resolveListen, reject) => {\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n.catch((error) => { console.error(error); response.writeHead(500).end(); });\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696586\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696587,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 61,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=368ff285-e739-4eda-b0b1-74cd98d571a2 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP3: The guard `toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(400)` does not verify the legacy management routes are removed because it also passes when they still exist but are protected by credentials. Under the old code the removed test showed an unauthenticated GET on the registration client URI returned 401, and an unauthenticated DELETE would likewise return 401 — both satisfy `>= 400`, so this test would pass unchanged on the pre-PR code and gives false confidence that the routes are gone. Assert the actual not-found status (404, returned by the app's `app.notFound` handler) so a re-introduced dynamic-management route fails this test.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts, line 61:\\n\\n<comment>The guard `toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(400)` does not verify the legacy management routes are removed because it also passes when they still exist but are protected by credentials. Under the old code the removed test showed an unauthenticated GET on the registration client URI returned 401, and an unauthenticated DELETE would likewise return 401 — both satisfy `>= 400`, so this test would pass unchanged on the pre-PR code and gives false confidence that the routes are gone. Assert the actual not-found status (404, returned by the app's `app.notFound` handler) so a re-introduced dynamic-management route fails this test.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -54,152 +54,20 @@ describe(\\\"OAuth 2.1 authorization server integration\\\", () => {\\n+    const registrationPath = `${OAUTH_ISSUER}/auth/oauth/register/${encodeURIComponent(client.clientId)}`;\\n+    expect(\\n+      (await environment.app.fetch(new Request(registrationPath))).status,\\n+    ).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(400);\\n+    expect(\\n+      (\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696587\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696588,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/metadata.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 12,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=5da73e50-694d-4576-a9a5-bdb4a3ceac0e -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP3: This broad return type removes the compile-time metadata contract from the exported function and forces consumers to narrow every standard field. Preserve McpFn’s generated shape with the helper’s return type.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/metadata.ts, line 12:\\n\\n<comment>This broad return type removes the compile-time metadata contract from the exported function and forces consumers to narrow every standard field. Preserve McpFn’s generated shape with the helper’s return type.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -1,60 +1,40 @@\\n-): AuthorizationServerMetadata {\\n-  return {\\n+  runtime: Pick<OAuthRuntime, \\\"issuer\\\" | \\\"resource\\\">,\\n+): Record<string, unknown> {\\n+  return createMcpAuthorizationServerMetadata({\\n     issuer: runtime.issuer,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n): ReturnType<typeof createMcpAuthorizationServerMetadata> {\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696588\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814263,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:24Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:25Z\",\n    \"path\": \".conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 12,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885666660,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. The tracked completion evidence now records McpFn 61a82af3c633332850cc1c128524507e42b8e72a and digest sha256:adaa175413235666da56f3850ce2d01905745777710a5ee99e01472cc28c1d6c, plus the current remediation gates.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814263\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814353,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:26Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:26Z\",\n    \"path\": \".conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 12,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696560,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Completion metadata, source pin, digest, artifact size, and verification results now reflect the final reviewed McpFn head.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814353\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814409,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:27Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:27Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 52,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675694,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Local-worktree verification now hashes package.json plus both src and built dist artifacts, so the digest covers the bytes consumed through package exports.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814409\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814469,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:28Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:28Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 50,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696549,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. The pinned digest now includes executable dist output for auth, core, and testing.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814469\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814523,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:29Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:30Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"original_line\": 150,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675696,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed across McpFn 61a82af3 and Skillplane 80acd42. McpFn now exposes a pre-client-resolution hook for authorization, token, and revocation; Skillplane applies network-only limits there before any registered or external metadata lookup.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814523\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814570,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:31Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:31Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 153,\n    \"original_line\": 109,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696550,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed across McpFn 61a82af3 and Skillplane 80acd42. Token lookup throttling is keyed by endpoint plus network, so varying an untrusted client_id cannot bypass it. Unit coverage proves two different remote client IDs share the bucket and never invoke fetch.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814570\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814625,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:32Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:32Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 61,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675700,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Removed registration-management routes now return an exact 404 stable error envelope.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814625\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815151,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:45Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:45Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 61,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675700,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Removed registration-management routes now return an exact 404 stable error envelope.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815151\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815202,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:46Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:46Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 61,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885678998,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. AuthFn routing now checks for a real route before delegation, preventing unknown removed routes from being converted to 500.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815202\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815232,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:47Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:47Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 61,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675700,\n    \"body\": \"Addressed in 80acd42 with exact 404 and ROUTE_NOT_FOUND assertions for both methods.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/actions/runs/33238273374/job/99063029666) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815232\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815233,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:47Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:47Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 61,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696587,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42 with exact GET and DELETE 404 assertions plus a unit test for the stable ROUTE_NOT_FOUND envelope.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815233\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815266,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:48Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:48Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 56,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885679003,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Digest labels normalize separators to forward slashes and package/file ordering uses bytewise code-unit comparison.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815266\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815307,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:49Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:49Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 56,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696571,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Locale-dependent sorting was removed and relative digest paths are platform-normalized.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815307\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815341,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:50Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:50Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 166,\n    \"original_line\": 121,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696552,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Refresh grants now pass through the shared oauth-token client-and-network limiter before the refresh-specific limiter.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815341\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815343,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:50Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:50Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 52,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675694,\n    \"body\": \"Addressed in 80acd42 by including each linked package's dist artifacts in the source digest.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/actions/runs/33238273374/job/99063029666) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815343\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815429,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:53Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:53Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"original_line\": 150,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675696,\n    \"body\": \"Addressed in 80acd42 with a pre-client-resolution network limiter and no-fetch coverage.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/actions/runs/33238273374/job/99063029666) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815429\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815751,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:05Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:05Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/src/auth.ts\",\n    \"line\": 253,\n    \"original_line\": 253,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696563,\n    \"body\": \"No code change needed. readBearerToken only performs URLSearchParams access and a header regex on a Web Request, so it does not throw for the valid Request accepted by this handler. Existing missing and malformed Bearer values fail closed; adding a catch here would hide unrelated programmer faults.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815751\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815769,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:06Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:06Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 10,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696574,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. The verifier invokes git through PATH instead of hardcoded macOS or Windows install paths.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815769\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815786,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:07Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:07Z\",\n    \"path\": \".conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json\",\n    \"line\": 21,\n    \"original_line\": 21,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696576,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Conformance evidence schema v2 records executable scenario baselines and a separately mapped exact emitted check-ID set, then asserts exact equality for every FAILURE and WARNING.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815786\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815821,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/tests/conformance/expected-failures.yml\",\n    \"line\": 23,\n    \"original_line\": 23,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696580,\n    \"body\": \"Resolved in 80acd42 after executing the suggested change. The runner baseline API requires scenario IDs, so check IDs in expected-failures.yml make the gate fail those three scenarios. The YAML therefore retains executable scenario IDs, while the test explicitly maps them to server-sse-multiple-streams-session, elicitation-sep1034-general, and elicitation-sep1330-general and enforces exact emitted-ID equality.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815821\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815836,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 184,\n    \"original_line\": 121,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696585,\n    \"body\": \"Already covered, so no duplicate validators were added. packages/api/tests/security/oauth.security.test.ts rejects remote cleartext, credential-bearing, fragment, and wildcard redirects; it also covers unregistered error redirects, implicit response type, unknown scopes, Basic client auth, PKCE, audience binding, replay, CSRF, rate limits, and token-family reuse. The focused OAuth security and integration run passed 24 tests.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815836\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815860,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:09Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:09Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/tests/conformance/mcp.official-conformance.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 89,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696586,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. The forwarding catch now writes the original stack or value to stderr before returning 500.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815860\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885816211,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:21Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:21Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/metadata.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 12,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696588,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. authorizationServerMetadata now returns ReturnType<typeof createMcpAuthorizationServerMetadata>.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885816211\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885816266,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:22Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:22Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/package.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 16,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675690,\n    \"body\": \"Not attempted and intentionally left open. The only published @mcpfn packages are 0.0.1 with npm gitHead e11bd81db6390dbc38303a5f3da6baadbaef0c8b; that source is thousands of changed lines behind the reviewed MCP-2 runtime and lacks required authorization features. Replacing the links would silently remove the adopted implementation. Package publication was not authorized, so this PR retains the exact pinned local worktree until matching releases exist.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885816266\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885816290,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:23Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:23Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/package.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 17,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885678997,\n    \"body\": \"Not attempted and intentionally left open. The only published @mcpfn packages are 0.0.1 with npm gitHead e11bd81db6390dbc38303a5f3da6baadbaef0c8b; that source is thousands of changed lines behind the reviewed MCP-2 runtime and lacks required authorization features. Replacing the links would silently remove the adopted implementation. Package publication was not authorized, so this PR retains the exact pinned local worktree until matching releases exist.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885816290\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885816308,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:24Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:24Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/package.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 24,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696546,\n    \"body\": \"Not attempted and intentionally left open. The only published @mcpfn packages are 0.0.1 with npm gitHead e11bd81db6390dbc38303a5f3da6baadbaef0c8b; that source is thousands of changed lines behind the reviewed MCP-2 runtime and lacks required authorization features. Replacing the links would silently remove the adopted implementation. Package publication was not authorized, so this PR retains the exact pinned local worktree until matching releases exist.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885816308\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885816336,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-0