-08-29T06:24:58Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:58Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 231,\n    \"original_line\": 220,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"80acd42e7ff1b83eb5c4934c7e9093cf991e97f0\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve the supported loopback issuer in local mode**\\n\\nWhen services use the repository's default local bindings (`RUNTIME_ENV: \\\"local\\\"` without an explicit issuer), `parseOAuthEndpoints` supplies `http://localhost:5700`; constructing this compatibility handler passes that value to McpFn, whose issuer contract rejects non-HTTPS issuers. The completion record confirms that eight standard integration suites now abort during setup for this reason, and the same path prevents the default local auth service from starting, so the documented `pnpm test:integration` release gate cannot pass. Configure the shared local/test binding with a supported issuer or preserve loopback-HTTP support at this boundary.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885817246\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885829995,\n    \"user\": \"coderabbitai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:31:54Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:31:54Z\",\n    \"path\": \"scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 56,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"f61b249b2dd68b2e37ac6a41d1a95f1c2e3e4c94\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885679003,\n    \"body\": \"`@thyaravind`, thank you. The reported path normalization and deterministic ordering issue is addressed.\\n\\n`@thyaravind` Thanks for confirming the fix. I couldn't resolve this review thread on the repository platform, so it remains open. Please retry or resolve it manually.\\n\\n<sub>You are interacting with an AI system.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885829995\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885830098,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:31:56Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:45:00Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/package.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 16,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"80acd42e7ff1b83eb5c4934c7e9093cf991e97f0\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=7ba3546f-27af-4c0c-8e03-12bf529f28f4 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=52373e77-50cb-4268-b996-af50e7b2d836 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: These newly added production `dependencies` use `link:` to a machine-local worktree path (`../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/...`). The path resolves outside the repository to `/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/{auth,core}`, which does not exist in a clean checkout, so `pnpm install` fails for CI and for every other developer. Because they are in `dependencies` (not `devDependencies`), the mcp worker build and deploy cannot run for anyone but the author's machine. Resolve the McpFn packages to exact published versions (per the upgrade policy in `mcpfn-source.json`) before merging, or register them as workspace packages instead of machine-local links.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/package.json, line 16:\\n\\n<comment>These newly added production `dependencies` use `link:` to a machine-local worktree path (`../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/...`). The path resolves outside the repository to `/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/{auth,core}`, which does not exist in a clean checkout, so `pnpm install` fails for CI and for every other developer. Because they are in `dependencies` (not `devDependencies`), the mcp worker build and deploy cannot run for anyone but the author's machine. Resolve the McpFn packages to exact published versions (per the upgrade policy in `mcpfn-source.json`) before merging, or register them as workspace packages instead of machine-local links.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@\\n     \\\"deploy:check\\\": \\\"wrangler deploy --config wrangler.jsonc --dry-run --outdir dist-worker\\\"\\n   },\\n   \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n+    \\\"@mcpfn/auth\\\": \\\"link:../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/auth\\\",\\n+    \\\"@mcpfn/core\\\": \\\"link:../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/core\\\",\\n     \\\"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f9bc1d8`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885830098\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885830100,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:31:56Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T07:23:03Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 140,\n    \"original_line\": 130,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"80acd42e7ff1b83eb5c4934c7e9093cf991e97f0\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=17f6ceb5-0f93-4e84-8ecc-009656e5e27f -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=52373e77-50cb-4268-b996-af50e7b2d836 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: When local bindings leave `runtime.issuer` at `http://localhost:5700`, `createMcpAuthorizationCompatibilityHandler` rejects the non-HTTPS issuer during setup. Configure the shared local/test binding with a supported issuer or explicitly preserve loopback-HTTP support