sourceDigest` from that worktree. Any checkout lacking this exact out-of-repo worktree at that relative location (another engineer, CI, or a repo at a different depth) makes `pnpm mcpfn:verify` and the build fail, and the recorded `baseCommit`/`sourceDigest` cannot be independently verified from the repository alone. The deterministic contract gate is therefore not reproducible outside the author's machine. Note also that the digest is computed over package.json, src, and dist (build output), so rebuilding the worktree changes the digest even with unchanged source. Since CI per the PR notes requires the exact published packages, this local-worktree pin is machine-coupled and should not be treated as a hermetic gate.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn-source.json, line 4:\\n\\n<comment>The pinned `sourceRoot` resolves outside the repository to `../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2`, and `scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs` runs `git -C <sourceRoot> rev-parse HEAD` and recomputes `sourceDigest` from that worktree. Any checkout lacking this exact out-of-repo worktree at that relative location (another engineer, CI, or a repo at a different depth) makes `pnpm mcpfn:verify` and the build fail, and the recorded `baseCommit`/`sourceDigest` cannot be independently verified from the repository alone. The deterministic contract gate is therefore not reproducible outside the author's machine. Note also that the digest is computed over package.json, src, and dist (build output), so rebuilding the worktree changes the digest even with unchanged source. Since CI per the PR notes requires the exact published packages, this local-worktree pin is machine-coupled and should not be treated as a hermetic gate.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\\n+{\\n+  \\\"schemaVersion\\\": 1,\\n+  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"local-worktree\\\",\\n+  \\\"sourceRoot\\\": \\\