record attributes the release gates to McpFn commit `6ba81463...` and digest `08de55b2...`, but `mcpfn-source.json` selects `8c79a068...` with digest `9c0919b6...`, so the retained evidence does not establish that the dependency revision actually consumed by this change passed the stated gates. Fresh evidence after the earlier fix is that subsequent repinning advanced `mcpfn-source.json` without updating these completion identifiers; rerun the gates against the selected revision and update the record together.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3886228816\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3886247923,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T10:08:10Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T10:08:11Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn-source.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 5,\n    \"commit_id\": \"894beef6b6c384ec2805c07861267fcbc200aad7\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"894beef6b6c384ec2805c07861267fcbc200aad7\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"This repin leaves the tracked completion evidence stale: it still certifies `6ba8146` and the prior digest at lines 11–12 and 59. Update that record with the current pin, digest, and verification result so the retained evidence describes the head being reviewed.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Reconcile the retained source-pin evidence\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `mcpfn-source.json:5` — advances the consumed worktree to `8c79a06806b55280e3ba82c0fdc93df7b49c3f3e` and its new digest.\\n- `.conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md:11` — still names `6ba81463825455bcaf074c3faa40122d9ffeeb03` and the old digest.\\n- `.conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md:59` — still records `pnpm mcpfn:verify` as passing only against the prior pin.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- The tracked completion record must identify the exact McpFn commit and digest consumed at this PR head and accurately record the corresponding verification result.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3886247923\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3886247932,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T10:08:10Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T10:08:11Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 245,\n    \"commit_id\": \"894beef6b6c384ec2805c07861267fcbc200aad7\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"894beef6b6c384ec2805c07861267fcbc200aad7\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"This test calls the helper directly, so it still passes if `safeAuthorizationResponse` stops invoking it; that production wiring is the regression this commit needs to protect. Exercise a Client ID Metadata Document through the compatibility route and grant flow so omitting persistence fails the test.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Cover metadata-document persistence at the production seam\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts:245` — verifies the helper's SQL in isolation.\\n- `packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts:120` — contains the only production call that projects the remote client before authorization.\\n- `packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/authorization.ts` and the grant tables — depend on that projection for later consent and code issuance.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- A test must fail if the compatibility `/oauth/authorize` path no longer persists a validated Client ID Metadata Document client before the AuthFn grant lifecycle uses it.\\n- The assertion should cover the persisted client and redirect set through authorization and, where practical, code exchange rather than invoking `persistClientMetadataDocument` directly.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3886247932\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3886513861,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T11:44:39Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T11:44:40Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn-source.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 5,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"This now consumes `5705aad`, but the PR publication boundary still says the exact pinned and release-gated commit is `8c79a06`. Update the PR description to the current commit so reviewers and the eventual package-publication step use the same source identity as `mcpfn-source.json` and the completion record.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3886513861\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3886520013,\n    \"user\": \"coderabbitai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T11:47:57Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:30Z\",\n    \"path\": \".conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 12,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"original_commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>🔎 Supported by static analysis</summary>\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\n#!/bin/bash\\nset -eu\\n\\nfile=\\\".conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md\\\"\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- completion record ---'\\ncat -n \\\"$file\\\"\\n\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- exact McpFn identities in repository ---'\\nrg -n -C 2 \\\\\\n  '6ba81463825455bcaf074c3faa40122d9ffeeb03|08de55b27a585c72066c930bae720e170e4031331eef65345765de881bf69f21|5705aada0b6667132b5de324999e1d40e4df638f|9c0919b61d87ca6c1619a6b56cdd65c62c4a3ac6c734166b29376a86f2f8e900' \\\\\\n  .conduct