"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: review paused by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\\n\\n## Walkthrough\\n\\nSkillplane adopts McpFn for MCP server declarations, authenticated request handling, OAuth compatibility, client normalization, conformance testing, source verification, and operational release procedures. Legacy dynamic-registration management and local metadata hydration are removed.\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n**McpFn adoption**\\n\\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\\n|---|---|\\n|**MCP declaration and authenticated request flow** <br> `mcp/package.json`, `mcp/src/*`, `mcp/tests/security/*`|The MCP server uses declarative McpFn tools. Requests use provider authentication, scope resolution, host validation, and authenticated session propagation.|\\n|**Hosted OAuth compatibility integration** <br> `packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/...`, `packages/auth/...`, `packages/api/tests/...`|OAuth authorization, token, revoke, registration, metadata, and client normalization use McpFn helpers. Legacy registration management and local metadata hydration are removed.|\\n|**Pinned adoption and conformance verification** <br> `mcpfn-source.json`, `scripts/*`, `mcp/tests/conformance/*`, `.conduct/verification/SKI-6/*`, `package.json`|The repository verifies pinned McpFn sources and linked dependencies. Shared scripts run contract and official conformance tests with an expected-failure baseline and recorded summary.|\\n|**Operations and completion records** <br> `docs/operations/*`, `.conduct/issue-completions/*`|Operations documents define McpFn ownership, release gates, provider proof, deployment integration, and rollback rules. The completion record lists verification results and remaining provider evidence.|\\n\\n**Estimated code review effort:** 4 (Complex) | ~60 minutes\\n\\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\\n**Merge Risk:** _🟡 Moderate_ · up to `a767b`\\n\\nThe PR shifts MCP transport and OAuth handling to McpFn and removes legacy registration-management routes. It still relies on unpublished local packages, so clean CI/install portability and merge readiness remain blocked until the exact packages are published; the conformance record also omits the dependency pin, and durable registrations lack an evidenced retry or cleanup lifecycle.\\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\\n\\n### Sequence Diagram(s)\\n\\n```mermaid\\nsequenceDiagram\\n  participant MCPClient\\n  participant MCPHandler\\n  participant McpFnAuth\\n  participant SkillplaneDeclaration\\n  participant ToolRuntime\\n  MCPClient->>MCPHandler: Send MCP request with bearer credential\\n  MCPHandler->>McpFnAuth: Authenticate credential and resolve scopes\\n  McpFnAuth-->>MCPHandler: Return authenticated principal\\n  MCPHandler->>SkillplaneDeclaration: Invoke declared operation\\n  SkillplaneDeclaration->>ToolRuntime: Dispatch validated tool input\\n  ToolRuntime-->>MCPClient: Return MCP result\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 4 | ❌ 1</summary>\\n\\n### ❌ Failed checks (1 warning)\\n\\n|     Check name     | Status     | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                               | Resolution                                                                         |\\n| :----------------: | :--------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Docstring Coverage | ⚠️ Warning | Docstring coverage is 1.56% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. Do