ves legacy registration-management paths, and adds authenticated conformance, source-integrity, operational, and rollback gates; controlled Claude and ChatGPT acceptance plus package publication and deployment remain pending.\\n\\n#### Sequence diagram for authenticated MCP request handling\\n\\n```mermaid\\nsequenceDiagram\\n    participant Client as MCP Client\\n    participant Worker as Skillplane MCP Worker\\n    participant McpFnAuth as McpFn Auth Handler\\n    participant AuthFn as Skillplane/AuthFn\\n    participant Server as McpFn Server\\n\\n    Client->>Worker: POST /mcp\\n    Worker->>McpFnAuth: createAuthProviderMcpHandler\\n    McpFnAuth->>AuthFn: authenticateMcpCredential\\n    AuthFn-->>McpFnAuth: provider credential and identity\\n    McpFnAuth->>McpFnAuth: requiredScopes\\n    McpFnAuth->>Worker: authInfo with skillplaneIdentity\\n    Worker->>Server: createWebStandardHandler\\n    Server-->>Worker: MCP response\\n    Worker-->>Client: authenticated tool result or scope challenge\\n```\\n\\n#### Flow diagram for McpFn adoption and release gates\\n\\n```mermaid\\nflowchart TD\\n    Pin[mcpfn:verify: pinned commit, digest, and links] --> Contract[test:mcp:contract]\\n    Contract --> Conformance[test:mcp:conformance]\\n    Conformance --> Suites[unit, integration, and security suites]\\n    Suites --> Build[typecheck and build]\\n    Build --> Provider[Controlled Claude and ChatGPT acceptance]\\n    Provider -->|both pass| Deploy[Paired app and MCP deployment]\\n    Provider -->|pending or fails| Hold[Hold release; retain bounded evidence]\\n    Deploy --> Rollback[Paired rollback: MCP Worker before app]\\n```\\n\\n### File-Level Changes\\n\\n| Change | Details | Files |\\n| ------ | ------- | ----- |\\n| Moves MCP protocol, transport, hosted OAuth, and credential-to-principal adaptation into McpFn while retaining Skillplane domain authorization and AuthFn persistence. | <ul><li>Defines the complete Skillplane tool catalog with McpFn declarations and Zod-derived schemas.</li><li>Uses McpFn’s provider-shaped authenticated handler and web-standard transport.</li><li>Adapts McpFn auth context back to server-derived Skillplane identity and required scopes.</li><li>Adds production Host validation and preserves stateless-session behavior.</li></ul> | `mcp/src/index.ts`<br/>`mcp/src/server.ts`<br/>`mcp/src/auth.ts`<br/>`mcp/package.json` |\\n| Delegates hosted OAuth protocol validation and metadata handling to McpFn and removes Skillplane’s legacy registration-management ownership. | <ul><li>Wraps AuthFn token, consent, persistence, and audit operations behind McpFn’s authorization compatibility contract.</li><li>Removes local OAuth request parsing, redirect validation, Client ID Metadata Document hydration, and registration access-token management.</li><li>Retains only Skillplane’s network allow-policy and registered-client persistence adapters.</li><li>Updates OAuth metadata, challenges, error mappings, and security/integration expectations.</li></ul> | `packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts`<br/>`packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/authorization.ts`<br/>`packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/clients.ts`<br/>`packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/metadata.ts`<br/>`packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/verify.ts`<br/>`packages/auth/src/oauth.ts`<br/>`packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/audit.ts`<br/>`packages/api/tests/integration/oauth.integration.test.ts`<br/>`packages/api/tests/security/oauth.security.test.ts`<br/>`packages/api/tests/support/oauth-test-environment.test.support.ts`<br/>`packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts` |\\n| Adds reproducible McpFn source pinning and adoption-boundary verification for the unpublished local dependency set. | <ul><li>Pins the McpFn worktree commit, package identities, and source digest.</li><li>Requires explicit local links to the pinned worktree.</li><li>Fails on runtime ownership regressions, retained legacy routes, or local metadata hydration.</li></ul> | `mcpfn-source.json`<br/>`scripts/verify-mcpfn-adoption.mjs`<br/>`pnpm-lock.yaml`<br/>`package.json` |\\n| Introduces separate deterministic MCP contract and authenticated official conformance gates with bounded evidence. | <ul><li>Adds a contract-test runner and an official conformance runner through an authenticated loopback proxy.</li><li>Baselines only reviewed non-advertised capabilities while keeping core protocol and DNS-rebinding checks hard-gated.</li><li>Scans and deletes raw artifacts, retaining a bounded redacted summary.</li></ul> | `scripts/run-mcp-contract.mjs`<br/>`scripts/run-mcp-conformance.mjs`<br/>`mcp/tests/conformance/mcp.official-conformance.test.ts`<br/>`mcp/tests/conformance/expected-failures.yml`<br/>`mcp/tests/conformance/mcp.conformance.test.ts`<br/>`mcp/tests/security/mcp-read.security.test.ts`<br/>`.conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json` |\\n| Documents operational ownership, release prerequisites, controlled provider acceptance, and paired rollback. | <ul><li>Documents McpFn versus Skillplane/AuthFn responsibilities and package replacement rules.</li><li>Defines required verification gates and pending Claude/ChatGPT controlled-development proof.</li><li>Requires paired app/MCP rollback and post-rollback OAuth and authenticated-tool smoke checks.</li></ul> | `docs/operations/mcpfn.md`<br/>`docs/operations/deployment.md`<br/>`docs/operations/rollback.md` |\\n| Records the draft completion status, validation evidence, publication boundary, and remaining acceptance work. | <ul><li>Captures the exact source pin and digest plus passing test, typecheck, build, and release-gate results.</li><li>Marks live provider verification and publication/deployment as out of scope and incomplete.</li><li>Records artifact hygiene and excluded unrelated work.</li></ul> | `.conduct/issue-completions/2026-08-27-ski6mcpf-completion.md` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Tips and commands</summary>\\n\\n#### Interacting with Sourcery\\n\\n- **Trigger a new review:** Comment `@sourcery-ai review` on the pull request.\\n- **Continue discussions:** Reply directly to Sourcery's review comments.\\n- **Generate a GitHub issue from a review comment:** Ask Sourcery to create an\\n  issue from a review comment by replying to it. You can also reply to a\\n  review comment with `@sourcery-ai issue` to create an issue from it.\\n- **Generate a pull request title:** Write `@sourcery-ai` anywhere in the pull\\n  request title to generate a title at any time. You can also comment\\n  `@sourcery-ai title` on the pull request to (re-)generate the title at any time.\\n- **Generate a pull request summary:** Write `@sourcery-ai summary` anywhere in\\n  the pull request body to generate a PR summary at any time exactly where you\\n  want it. You can also comment `@sourcery-ai summary` on the pull request to\\n  (re-)generate the summary at any time.\\n- **Generate reviewer's guide:** Comment `@sourcery-ai guide` on the pull\\n  request to (re-)generate the reviewer's guide at any time.\\n- **Resolve all Sourcery comments:** Comment `@sourcery-ai resolve` on the\\n  pull request to resolve all Sourcery comments. Useful if you've already\\n  addressed all the comments and don't want to see them anymore.\\n- **Dismiss all Sourcery reviews:** Comment `@sourcery-ai dismiss` on the pull\\n  request to dismiss all existing Sourcery reviews. Especially useful if you\\n  want to start fresh with a new review - don't forget to comment\\n  `@sourcery-ai review` to trigger a new review!\\n\\n#### Customizing Your Experience\\n\\nAccess your [dashboard](https://app.sourcery.ai) to:\\n- Enable or disable review features such as the Sourcery-generated pull request\\n  summary, the reviewer's guide, and others.\\n- Change the review language.\\n- Add, remove or edit custom review instructions.\\n- Adjust other review settings.\\n\\n#### Getting Help\\n\\n- [Contact our support team](mailto:support@sourcery.ai) for questions or feedback.\\n- Visit our [documentation](https://docs.sourcery.ai) for detailed guides and information.\\n- Keep in touch with the Sourcery team by following us on [X/Twitter](https://x.com/SourceryAI), [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/sourcery-ai/) or [GitHub](https://github.com/sourcery-ai).\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<!-- Generated by sourcery-ai[bot]: end review_guide -->\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#issuecomment-5452126022\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"qodo-code-review\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T05:08:14Z\",\n      \"updatedAt\": null,\n      \"body\": \"### Qodo reviews are paused for this user.\\n\\nTroubleshooting steps vary by plan [Learn more →](https://docs.qodo.ai/subscription-plans#what-you%E2%80%99ll-see-when-reviews-are-paused)\\n\\n\\n**On a Teams plan?**\\nReviews resume once this user has a paid seat *and* their Git account is linked in Qodo.\\n[Link Git account →](https://docs.qodo.ai/subscription-plans#linking-a-git-account)\\n\\n**Using GitHub Enterprise Server, GitLab Self-Managed, or Bitbucket Data Center?**\\nThese require an Enterprise plan - Contact us\\n[Contact us →](https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-support#support)\\n\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#issuecomment-5460491228\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T05:08:21Z\",\n      \"updatedAt\": null,\n      \"body\": \"<!-- codex-pull-request-review-summary -->\\n\\n## Codex Review Summary\\n\\nThis comment shows the latest Codex review activity on this pull request.\\n\\n| Review | Status | Commit | Review trigger |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| 📝 **Code Review** | ✅ **Completed** <relative-time datetime=\\\"2026-08-29T12:48:38.814861Z\\\">2026-08-29T12:48:38.814861Z</relative-time> | `f9bc1d8` | New commits |\\n\\n\\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\" or \\\"@codex security review\\\".\\n\\nCodex reacts with 👀 while any review is running, comments if it has suggestions, and reacts with 👍 once all reviews finish with no findings.\\n\\n</details>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#issuecomment-5460491665\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"thyaravind\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:50Z\",\n      \"updatedAt\": null,\n      \"body\": \"One bounded review-remediation round is complete at `80acd42`, pinned to McpFn `61a82af3c633332850cc1c128524507e42b8e72a` with digest `sha256:adaa175413235666da56f3850ce2d01905745777710a5ee99e01472cc28c1d6c`.\\n\\nFixed:\\n- pre-client-resolution network rate limits and refresh shared-token limiting\\n- verifier coverage of built `dist` bytes, portable Git lookup, bytewise ordering, normalized paths\\n- exact removed-route 404 behavior and assertions\\n- exact conformance scenario-to-check evidence reconciliation and forwarding error logging\\n- metadata return typing and completion evidence\\n\\nSkipped / already covered:\\n- malformed Bearer parsing does not throw for a valid Web Request and already fails closed\\n- OAuth redirect, grant, scope, confidential-client, replay, CSRF, audience, rate-limit, and leakage security coverage already exists; focused OAuth integration/security passed 24 tests\\n\\nNot attempted:\\n- five local-link replacement threads remain open. Published `@mcpfn/*@0.0.1` has npm `gitHead=e11bd81db6390dbc38303a5f3da6baadbaef0c8b` and predates the required MCP-2 runtime. Publishing matching packages was not authorized.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- `pnpm mcpfn:verify` passed\\n- MCP contract 8/8; authenticated conformance 1/1\\n- full typecheck 29/29 tasks\\n- Auth/AuthFn OAuth units and focused API OAuth integration/security passed\\n\\nThe broad integration command also exposed eight unrelated suite setup failures from a shared non-HTTPS default OAuth issuer; those suites did not run test bodies. The changed OAuth integration suite passed after the route fix. No merge, deployment, or package publication was performed.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#issuecomment-5460801481\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"thyaravind\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T07:23:20Z\",\n      \"updatedAt\": null,\n      \"body\": \"One bounded pr-refetch-fix round is complete at f512980e42247b92388bc72185d92f9869ce51fa, pinned to McpFn 6ba81463825455bcaf074c3faa40122d9ffeeb03 with digest sha256:08de55b27a585c72066c930bae720e170e4031331eef65345765de881bf69f21.\\n\\nFixed and resolved:\\n- controlled localhost issuer support; the previously aborted API suites now start and pass\\n- required dynamic-registration client names\\n- direct-pnpm MCP test execution\\n- dependency-section and AST-backed reachable-module adoption verification\\n- endpoint-and-network rate-limit coverage plus accurate revocation errors\\n- pre-read conformance artifact-size gating and deterministic tracked summary output\\n- stale PR pin, readiness, and validation metadata\\n- both Sonar annotations in the snapshotted failed check\\n\\nVerification:\\n- McpFn adoption gate passed\\n- MCP contract 8/8; authenticated conformance 1/1\\n- full typecheck 29/29 tasks\\n- full integration 24/24 tasks\\n- focused OAuth security 17/17\\n- changed-file lint, Prettier, and git diff checks passed\\n\\nNot attempted and intentionally left open:\\n- eight local-link/source-root threads. Matching McpFn artifacts are not published; the requested boundary is the latest exact local worktree, and package publication was not authorized.\\n\\nRepository-wide lint still scans generated docs/.next, docs/.open-next, and docs/.source output and fails there; the changed files lint cleanly. No merge, deployment, package publication, live-provider run, or Linear status transition was performed.\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#issuecomment-5461040250\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"socket-security\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:47Z\",\n      \"updatedAt\": null,\n      \"body\": \"**Review the following changes in direct dependencies.** Learn more about [Socket for GitHub](https://socket.dev?utm_medium=gh).\\n\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Diff</th>\\n<th width=\\\"200px\\\">Package</th>\\n<th align=\\\"center\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Supply Chain<br/>Security</th>\\n<th align=\\\"center\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Vulnerability</th>\\n<th align=\\\"center\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Quality</th>\\n<th align=\\\"center\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">Maintenance</th>\\n<th align=\\\"center\\\" width=\\\"100px\\\">License</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr><td align=\\\"center\\\"><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/ea8a387a-1e64-40ae-ae36-799d24a3400d?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101941811703\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github-app-statics.socket.dev/diff-added.svg\\\" title=\\\"Added\\\" alt=\\\"Added\\\" width=\\\"20\\\" height=\\\"20\\\"></a></td><td><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/ea8a387a-1e64-40ae-ae36-799d24a3400d?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101941811703\\\">@​mcpfn/​testing@​0.0.2</a></td><td align=\\\"center\\\"><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/ea8a387a-1e64-40ae-ae36-799d24a3400d?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101941811703\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github-app-statics.socket.dev/score-76.svg\\\" title=\\\"Supply Chain Security\\\" width=\\\"40\\\" height=\\\"40\\\" alt=\\\"76\\\"></a></td><td align=\\\"center\\\"><a href=\\\"https://socket.dev/dashboard/org/21n/diff-scan/ea8a387a-1e64-40ae-ae36-799d24a3400d?tab=dependencies&dependency_item_key=101941811703\\\"><img src=\\\"https://github-app-statics.socket.dev/score-100.svg\\\" title=\\\"Vulnerability\\\" width=\\\"40\\\" height=\\\"40\\\" alt=\\\"100\\\"></a></td