-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (the `-defaults`/`-enums` IDs do not appear anywhere in `result.checks`). Because the `interpretation` field claims exit code zero means every failure or warning belongs to the documented baseline, two actual failures are left outside the baseline list and two listed entries reference non-existent check IDs. Update the two elicitation IDs to the `-general` variants actually reported by the runner so the summary accurately documents the conformance baseline.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At .conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json, line 21:\\n\\n<comment>The `expectedFailureScenarios` list does not match the actual failing checks in the same document. It names `elicitation-sep1034-defaults` and `elicitation-sep1330-enums`, but the checks array reports FAILURE for `elicitation-sep1034-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (the `-defaults`/`-enums` IDs do not appear anywhere in `result.checks`). Because the `interpretation` field claims exit code zero means every failure or warning belongs to the documented baseline, two actual failures are left outside the baseline list and two listed entries reference non-existent check IDs. Update the two elicitation IDs to the `-general` variants actually reported by the runner so the summary accurately documents the conformance baseline.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@\\n+    \\\"tools-call-sampling\\\",\\n+    \\\"tools-call-elicitation\\\",\\n+    \\\"server-sse-multiple-streams\\\",\\n+    \\\"elicitation-sep1034-defaults\\\",\\n+    \\\"elicitation-sep1330-enums\\\",\\n+    \\\"resources-list\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    \\\"elicitation-sep1034-general\\\",\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696576\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696580,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:19Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/tests/conformance/expected-failures.yml\",\n    \"line\": 23,\n    \"original_line\": 23,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=6f7847df-9c0a-4408-8d58-85250473f5e0 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: The expected-failure scenario ids here do not match the ids recorded by the actual conformance run in `.conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json`. Three entries are wrong: the summary records FAILURE ids `elicitation-sep1034-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (not `elicitation-sep1034-defaults` / `elicitation-sep1330-enums`), and the baselined SSE warning id is `server-sse-multiple-streams-session` (not `server-sse-multiple-streams`). The file comment says the SSE session warning is baselined explicitly, so the entry is missing its `-session` suffix. Because the baseline id is not the id the runner emitted, the gate either does not actually baseline the intended scenario (exact match) or baselines a name that never occurs, so the recorded \\\"every failure/warning belongs to the baseline\\\" evidence does not reconcile with these entries. Align each entry with the exact scenario ids emitted by the conformance runner and re-verify the gate stays green.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/tests/conformance/expected-failures.yml, line 21:\\n\\n<comment>The expected-failure scenario ids here do not match the ids recorded by the actual conformance run in `.conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json`. Three entries are wrong: the summary records FAILURE ids `elicitation-sep1034-general` and `elicitation-sep1330-general` (not `elicitation-sep1034-defaults` / `elicitation-sep1330-enums`), and the baselined SSE warning id is `server-sse-multiple-streams-session` (not `server-sse-multiple-streams`). The file comment says the SSE session warning is baselined explicitly, so the entry is missing its `-session` suffix. Because the baseline id is not the id the runner emitted, the gate either does not actually baseline the intended scenario (exact match) or baselines a name that never occurs, so the recorded \\\"every failure/warning belongs to the baseline\\\" evidence does not reconcile with these entries. Align each entry with the exact scenario ids emitted by the conformance runner and re-verify the gate stays green.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\\n+  - tools-call-with-progress\\n+  - tools-call-sampling\\n+  - tools-call-elicitation\\n+  - server-sse-multiple-streams\\n+  - elicitation-sep1034-defaults\\n+  - elicitation-sep1330-enums\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  - server-sse-multiple-streams-session\\n  - elicitation-sep1034-general\\n  - elicitation-sep1330-general\\n\\n```\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696580\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696583,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:58Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn-source.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 4,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=be7e1605-43b2-461a-8a15-e496f8ceb296 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} -->\\nP2: This pin and the `link:` dependencies it backs (mcp/package.json, packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/package.json) resolve to an external local worktree at `../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2`, which is outside the repository and not part of the checkout. `pnpm mcpfn:verify` runs `git -C <sourceRoot> rev-parse HEAD` and immediately throws, and `pnpm install` resolves each `link:` to a nonexistent directory. A clean checkout on any other machine or CI runner can therefore neither install/build nor pass the adoption gate — nothing in the repo or lockfile makes the pinned source reproducible. The draft-boundary limitation is acknowledged in the PR, but as written this file makes the committed state non-buildable; keep it as a draft-only boundary or vendor the exact commit into the repo until the published-package replacement lands.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn-source.json, line 4:\\n\\n<comment>This pin and the `link:` dependencies it backs (mcp/package.json, packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/package.json) resolve to an external local worktree at `../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2`, which is outside the repository and not part of the checkout. `pnpm mcpfn:verify` runs `git -C <sourceRoot> rev-parse HEAD` and immediately throws, and `pnpm install` resolves each `link:` to a nonexistent directory. A clean checkout on any other machine or CI runner can therefore neither install/build nor pass the adoption gate — nothing in the repo or lockfile makes the pinned source reproducible. The draft-boundary limitation is acknowledged in the PR, but as written this file makes the committed state non-buildable; keep it as a draft-only boundary or vendor the exact commit into the repo until the published-package replacement lands.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\\n+{\\n+  \\\"schemaVersion\\\": 1,\\n+  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"local-worktree\\\",\\n+  \\\"sourceRoot\\\": \\\"../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2\\\",\\n+  \\\"baseCommit\\\": \\\"42a0f2c3876adb47fb26dfc187f6fea41f436719\\\",\\n+  \\\"sourceDigest\\\": \\\"sha256:445472059355d481bbf34022dceea6b86ae4cc452562ca628109a8c7e9e509f3\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f9bc1d8`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696583\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885696585,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T05:27:20Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 184,\n    \"original_line\": 121,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=d050964c-66a1-46c3-8faa-39b519b6fb56 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=cb01c544-8d69-47f1-9759-76fe0b2e2303 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} -->\\nP2: The replacement redirect test drops most of the previous security coverage. The old `validateRedirectUri` suite rejected redirect URIs with userinfo credentials, URL fragments, and wildcard hosts, and the removed `validateRegistration` test asserted that confidential auth methods, non-code response types, password/other grants, and non-allowlisted scopes are rejected. The new `normalizeMcpClientRegistration` test only covers a single unsafe HTTP redirect URI plus one loopback/HTTPS normalization, so a regression in McpFn rejecting credentials, fragments, wildcards, client_secret_basic, implicit/password grants, or unknown scopes would not be caught. Restore equivalent rejection coverage for this security boundary.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts, line 121:\\n\\n<comment>The replacement redirect test drops most of the previous security coverage. The old `validateRedirectUri` suite rejected redirect URIs with userinfo credentials, URL fragments, and wildcard hosts, and the removed `validateRegistration` test asserted that confidential auth methods, non-code response types, password/other grants, and non-allowlisted scopes are rejected. The new `normalizeMcpClientRegistration` test only covers a single unsafe HTTP redirect URI plus one loopback/HTTPS normalization, so a regression in McpFn rejecting credentials, fragments, wildcards, client_secret_basic, implicit/password grants, or unknown scopes would not be caught. Restore equivalent rejection coverage for this security boundary.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -119,25 +118,28 @@ describe(\\\"OAuth 2.1 metadata and configuration\\\", () => {\\n-      \\\"https://agent.example.test/callback?source=mcp\\\",\\n-    );\\n-    expect(validateRedirectUri(\\\"http://127.0.0.1:49152/callback\\\")).toBe(\\n+  it(\\\"delegates exact HTTPS and loopback redirect normalization to McpFn\\\", () => {\\n+    const registration = normalizeMcpClientRegistration({\\n+      clientId: \\\"client\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885696585\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814523,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:29Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:30Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"original_line\": 150,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675696,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed across McpFn 61a82af3 and Skillplane 80acd42. McpFn now exposes a pre-client-resolution hook for authorization, token, and revocation; Skillplane applies network-only limits there before any registered or external metadata lookup.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814523\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885814570,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:31Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:31Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 153,\n    \"original_line\": 109,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696550,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed across McpFn 61a82af3 and Skillplane 80acd42. Token lookup throttling is keyed by endpoint plus network, so varying an untrusted client_id cannot bypass it. Unit coverage proves two different remote client IDs share the bucket and never invoke fetch.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885814570\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815341,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:50Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:50Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 166,\n    \"original_line\": 121,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696552,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Refresh grants now pass through the shared oauth-token client-and-network limiter before the refresh-specific limiter.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815341\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815429,\n    \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:53Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:23:53Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 195,\n    \"original_line\": 150,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885675696,\n    \"body\": \"Addressed in 80acd42 with a pre-client-resolution network limiter and no-fetch coverage.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/actions/runs/33238273374/job/99063029666) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815429\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815751,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:05Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:05Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/src/auth.ts\",\n    \"line\": 253,\n    \"original_line\": 253,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696563,\n    \"body\": \"No code change needed. readBearerToken only performs URLSearchParams access and a header regex on a Web Request, so it does not throw for the valid Request accepted by this handler. Existing missing and malformed Bearer values fail closed; adding a catch here would hide unrelated programmer faults.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815751\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815786,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:07Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:07Z\",\n    \"path\": \".conduct/verification/SKI-6/official-conformance-summary.json\",\n    \"line\": 21,\n    \"original_line\": 21,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696576,\n    \"body\": \"Fixed in 80acd42. Conformance evidence schema v2 records executable scenario baselines and a separately mapped exact emitted check-ID set, then asserts exact equality for every FAILURE and WARNING.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815786\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815821,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/tests/conformance/expected-failures.yml\",\n    \"line\": 23,\n    \"original_line\": 23,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696580,\n    \"body\": \"Resolved in 80acd42 after executing the suggested change. The runner baseline API requires scenario IDs, so check IDs in expected-failures.yml make the gate fail those three scenarios. The YAML therefore retains executable scenario IDs, while the test explicitly maps them to server-sse-multiple-streams-session, elicitation-sep1034-general, and elicitation-sep1330-general and enforces exact emitted-ID equality.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815821\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885815836,\n    \"user\": \"thyaravind\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:08Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/oauth.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 184,\n    \"original_line\": 121,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": 3885696585,\n    \"body\": \"Already covered, so no duplicate validators were added. packages/api/tests/security/oauth.security.test.ts rejects remote cleartext, credential-bearing, fragment, and wildcard redirects; it also covers unregistered error redirects, implicit response type, unknown scopes, Basic client auth, PKCE, audience binding, replay, CSRF, rate limits, and token-family reuse. The focused OAuth security and integration run passed 24 tests.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885815836\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885817246,\n    \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:58Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:24:58Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 231,\n    \"original_line\": 220,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve the supported loopback issuer in local mode**\\n\\nWhen services use the repository's default local bindings (`RUNTIME_ENV: \\\"local\\\"` without an explicit issuer), `parseOAuthEndpoints` supplies `http://localhost:5700`; constructing this compatibility handler passes that value to McpFn, whose issuer contract rejects non-HTTPS issuers. The completion record confirms that eight standard integration suites now abort during setup for this reason, and the same path prevents the default local auth service from starting, so the documented `pnpm test:integration` release gate cannot pass. Configure the shared local/test binding with a supported issuer or preserve loopback-HTTP support at this boundary.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885817246\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885830098,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:31:56Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:45:00Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcp/package.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"original_line\": 16,\n    \"commit_id\": \"a767b057d162d8a067f33c21ae9a09a29122cb97\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=7ba3546f-27af-4c0c-8e03-12bf529f28f4 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=52373e77-50cb-4268-b996-af50e7b2d836 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: These newly added production `dependencies` use `link:` to a machine-local worktree path (`../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/...`). The path resolves outside the repository to `/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/{auth,core}`, which does not exist in a clean checkout, so `pnpm install` fails for CI and for every other developer. Because they are in `dependencies` (not `devDependencies`), the mcp worker build and deploy cannot run for anyone but the author's machine. Resolve the McpFn packages to exact published versions (per the upgrade policy in `mcpfn-source.json`) before merging, or register them as workspace packages instead of machine-local links.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcp/package.json, line 16:\\n\\n<comment>These newly added production `dependencies` use `link:` to a machine-local worktree path (`../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/...`). The path resolves outside the repository to `/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/{auth,core}`, which does not exist in a clean checkout, so `pnpm install` fails for CI and for every other developer. Because they are in `dependencies` (not `devDependencies`), the mcp worker build and deploy cannot run for anyone but the author's machine. Resolve the McpFn packages to exact published versions (per the upgrade policy in `mcpfn-source.json`) before merging, or register them as workspace packages instead of machine-local links.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@\\n     \\\"deploy:check\\\": \\\"wrangler deploy --config wrangler.jsonc --dry-run --outdir dist-worker\\\"\\n   },\\n   \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n+    \\\"@mcpfn/auth\\\": \\\"link:../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/auth\\\",\\n+    \\\"@mcpfn/core\\\": \\\"link:../../../../worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/core\\\",\\n     \\\"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f9bc1d8`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885830098\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885830100,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:31:56Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T07:23:03Z\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts\",\n    \"line\": 140,\n    \"original_line\": 130,\n    \"commit_id\": \"f9bc1d86e76054f6e3d6c11a3082fe5d20235392\",\n    \"in_reply_to_id\": null,\n    \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=17f6ceb5-0f93-4e84-8ecc-009656e5e27f -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=52373e77-50cb-4268-b996-af50e7b2d836 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: When local bindings leave `runtime.issuer` at `http://localhost:5700`, `createMcpAuthorizationCompatibilityHandler` rejects the non-HTTPS issuer during setup. Configure the shared local/test binding with a supported issuer or explicitly preserve loopback-HTTP support so the default auth service and integration gate can start.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/authfn-mcp-oauth/src/plugin.ts, line 130:\\n\\n<comment>When local bindings leave `runtime.issuer` at `http://localhost:5700`, `createMcpAuthorizationCompatibilityHandler` rejects the non-HTTPS issuer during setup. Configure the shared local/test binding with a supported issuer or explicitly preserve loopback-HTTP support so the default auth service and integration gate can start.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -3,211 +3,204 @@ import {\\n-    client_id_issued_at: client.clientIdIssuedAt,\\n-    registration_access_token: client.registrationAccessToken,\\n-    registration_client_uri: client.registrationClientUri,\\n+    issuer: runtime.issuer,\\n+    endpointPrefix: \\\"/auth/oauth\\\",\\n+    clients: {\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`f512980`](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/commit/f512980e42247b92388bc72185d92f9869ce51fa)\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/7#discussion_r3885830100\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": 3885830103,\n    \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-29T06:31:56Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-29T12:44:56Z\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn-source.json\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"o