{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T14:21:58.061Z","ordinal":15953,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a041ae-ce65-7631-a9e6-9a4d22e9067d","turn_id":"01a04de4-b2d2-7b13-8755-cb4387b230b8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-10d878df-dda7-4698-84d4-e80567746d7e","process_id":"4297","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md | sed -n '1,140p'\ngit status --short"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/skillplane-mcpfn-registry.6Caz55","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"nl -ba /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md | sed -n '1,140p'\ngit status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"     1\tthread_id: 01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b\n     2\tupdated_at: 2026-08-23T17:34:36+00:00\n     3\trollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T12-55-41-01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b.jsonl\n     4\tcwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane\n     5\tgit_branch: SKI-8\n     6\t\n     7\t# Bounded hosted Skillplane PR review-fix rounds for PR #3\n     8\t\n     9\tRollout context: In `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane`, the user repeatedly invoked `splane pr-review-fix` for `21nCo/skillplane` PR #3. The live Skillplane workflow resolved to `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` (published digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`). It mandates one bounded review snapshot, exact PR worktree validation, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and no post-push review refetch or CI loop.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Task 1: Initial report-and-fix review of PR #3\n    12\t\n    13\tOutcome: success\n    14\t\n    15\tPreference signals:\n    16\t\n    17\t- The user’s `splane pr review fixes PR #3` invocation was interpreted as a request to use the hosted Skillplane workflow, not local instructions or memory -> future `splane <skill>` commands should resolve and retrieve the live published skill first.\n    18\t- The workflow and prior user conventions required preserving a dirty checkout, using an exact-head dedicated worktree, and not overwriting unrelated artifacts -> review work was isolated at `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review` while the dirty `SKI-8` checkout remained untouched.\n    19\t- The hosted `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0` instructions required writing a raw evidence export and report before source edits, leaving code changes unstaged, and avoiding GitHub mutations; later `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` explicitly authorized one commit and push -> distinguish these workflow variants before acting.\n    20\t\n    21\tKey steps:\n    22\t\n    23\t- Discovered workspace `21n` via live Skillplane MCP and resolved `report-and-fix-pr@1.0.0`.\n    24\t- Confirmed PR #3 is `21nCo/skillplane`, head branch `SKI-1`, starting head `45733752797a5de552a447560983d24a9d02bcd1`; created a detached exact-head worktree.\n    25\t- Fetched all review surfaces once: 35 changed files, 21 inline comments, 6 submitted reviews, and 6 conversation comments. Stored `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n    26\t- Deduplicated review findings and validated them against current code. Addressed the then-current findings around rollup preservation, repeatable-read stats testing, and migration/application compatibility locking.\n    27\t- Added commit `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2` (`fix(review): harden stats rollout compatibility`) and pushed it to `SKI-1`.\n    28\t\n    29\tReusable knowledge:\n    30\t\n    31\t- PR #3 concerns AuthFn-backed service-principal credentials, public usage statistics, analytics rollups, and production deployment safety.\n    32\t- The repository’s production migration runner wraps migrations in transactions; migration `0019_public_stats_counter_shards.sql` changes public stats from one global counter to workspace shards. The implemented deployment guard records `applicationCommit` in production migration state and requires the deployment source commit to match it, preventing older binaries from running against the migrated schema.\n    33\t- Rollup preservation must use `existing.source_event_count >= eventCount` and return the persisted count, otherwise retention can erase fuller historical snapshots or make `RollupResult.sourceEvents` inconsistent.\n    34\t- The public-stats integration test previously held `LOCK TABLE skills IN SHARE MODE` across an HTTP request. The fix used a repeatable-read transaction and a same-connection app service provider; a read-only transaction failed because API middleware writes rate-limit state, so writable repeatable-read is required.\n    35\t- Focused validation passed: audit analytics 3/3, public-skills 5/5, observability tests 5/5, typechecks, lint/format/diff checks, full unit suite 28/28 Turbo tasks and 23/23 script tests.\n    36\t\n    37\tFailures and how to do differently:\n    38\t\n    39\t- An initial raw-export patch failed because the generated `apply_patch` string lacked the exact final `*** End Patch` line; retry with a correctly terminated patch.\n    40\t- A same-connection test attempt returned 503 because `createApiApp` requires `getServices`, not a services object. A second attempt returned 500 because `READ ONLY` blocked middleware writes. Correct wiring plus writable repeatable-read produced the passing test.\n    41\t- The immediate PR metadata check after push still showed the prior SHA even though local and remote refs matched. Do not poll or refetch in a bounded round; report the refresh lag honestly.\n    42\t\n    43\tReferences:\n    44\t\n    45\t- Hosted workflow: `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1`, digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`.\n    46\t- PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n    47\t- Worktree: `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane-pr-3-review`.\n    48\t- Report export: `.conduct/pr-reports/21nCo-skillplane-pr-3-comments.json`.\n    49\t- Commit: `996aebec59dcf66269dc9285d577d85267facdd2`.\n    50\t\n    51\t## Task 2: Follow-up bounded review round\n    52\t\n    53\tOutcome: success\n    54\t\n    55\tPreference signals:\n    56\t\n    57\t- The user invoked `splane pr-review-fix` again, implicitly requesting another bounded hosted round rather than an open-ended loop -> fetch once, fix once, push once, and terminate.\n    58\t\n    59\tKey steps:\n    60\t\n    61\t- Retrieved the current published `pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` skill again and verified clean `SKI-1` worktree/local/remote head at `996aebe...`.\n    62\t- Current review snapshot identified one actionable test gap: the compatibility test title claimed coverage for an unversioned application, but the test only covered an unversioned migration record.\n    63\t- Added an assertion calling `assertMigrationApplicationCompatibility({ applicationCommit: \"a\".repeat(40) })` without an application argument.\n    64\t- Ran formatting, lint, diff checks, and focused deployment tests (2/2 passed).\n    65\t- Created and pushed exactly one commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6` (`test(review): cover unversioned application deploys`). Local and remote matched; immediate PR metadata again lagged.\n    66\t\n    67\tReferences:\n    68\t\n    69\t- Added test: `scripts/production-deployment.test.mjs`.\n    70\t- Commit: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n    71\t\n    72\t## Task 3: Final bounded review round\n    73\t\n    74\tOutcome: success\n    75\t\n    76\tKey steps:\n    77\t\n    78\t- Retrieved the hosted workflow again and verified the dedicated worktree was clean with local, remote, and PR head all at `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n    79\t- Fetched review threads and supplementary surfaces once. There were 18 unresolved threads, but 7 were outdated; the current recent test comment was marked addressed by `d398cba`.\n    80\t- Read current code for remaining threads. No new actionable findings were found, so no files changed, commit was created, or push performed.\n    81\t\n    82\tReusable knowledge:\n    83\t\n    84\t- Unresolved GitHub thread status alone is insufficient: inspect `outdated`, current commit, current code, and explicit addressed markers. Current threads may be historical but already fixed or intentionally retained contracts.\n    85\t- Remaining not-attempted/intentional items included local expiry delegation to AuthFn, immutable applied migrations, and inability to reconstruct irrecoverable pre-counter historical data.\n    86\t\n    87\tReferences:\n    88\t\n    89\t- Final PR head: `d398cba6d93a46d9bb297ade58eba59808aee5a6`.\n    90\t- Final PR: `https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/3`.\n    91\t- Final result: no-op round; no tests rerun because no files changed.\n    92\t\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"     1\tthread_id: 01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b\n     2\tupdated_at: 2026-08-23T17:34:36+00:00\n     3\trollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T12-55-41-01a02d82-ccc1-7683-926d-46dfe638708b.jsonl\n     4\tcwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane\n     5\tgit_branch: SKI-8\n     6\t\n     7\t# Bounded hosted Skillplane PR review-fix rounds for PR #3\n     8\t\n     9\tRollout context: In `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane`, the user repeatedly invoked `splane pr-review-fix` for `21nCo/skillplane` PR #3. The live Skillplane workflow resolved to `21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1` (published digest `sha256:dc1151aeb9ef44d38c502b5f2eb17fca6fd89fb5653d022e07c0fd40f664143d`). It mandates one bounded review snapshot, exact PR worktree validation, narrow fixes, proportionate verification, at most one commit/push, and no post-push review refetch or CI loop.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Task 1: Initial report-and-fix review of PR #3\n    12\t\n    13\tOutcome: success\n    14\t\n 